FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://prodapi.shipox.com

# Shipox.com API Documentation

## Creating API Account

1. Contact your Account Manager who is a Shipox.com representative, or contact support@shipox.com, info@shipox.com to request for Merchant API Account creation.
2. Your Account Manager will provide you with test and live environment access details for API, including the host_name for each environment.
3. Once you have the access details and host_name provided, you can follow the rest of the documentation and request examples to use the API

##  HTTP Request Errors 


| Error Value | Error Message | Code |
| ----------- | ------------- | ---- |
| Access Denied | Doesn’t have token or expired | 401 |
| Forbidden | Doesn’t have permission | 403 |
| amount | Value can not be lower than 0 | 400 |
| locations | Can not create order without sender or recipient locations | 400 |
| locations | There can be only one pickup and drop-off location | 400 |
| locations | Provide either lat and lon coordinates or city for pickup location | 400 |
| locations | Provide either lat and lon coordinates or city for drop-off location | 400 |
| locations | Provided sender city code and/or country id is not valid (Check <a href="#countries">Cities\Countries API<a/>) | 400 |
| locations | Provided recipient city code and/or country id is not valid (Check <a href="#countries">Cities\Countries API</a>) | 400 |
| payer | Only sender can be a payer when payment type is credit card | 400 |
| recipient_not_available | We can’t leave the item to anyone if there is Cash to collect | 400 |
| credit_balance_not_active | `credit_balance` payment type is not activated | 400 |
| credit_balance | Sorry, you have reached `credit_balance` limit, select another payment type | 400 |
| package | Same Day delivery is available for pickup between 10:00 and 16:00. Please try to select another service type or schedule parcel pickup to another date | 400 |
| package | Package price with provided parameters not found (Check <a href="#service_type">Service Types</a> and <a href="#package_rules">Starting From API</a>) | 400 |
| status | Status can not be `Unassigned` when driver is selected | 400 |
| status | Status can not be `Assigned To Courier` when driver is selected | 400 |
| charge_item | You cannot provide more than two charge items | 400 |
| charge_item | You cannot provide two charge items with the same charge types | 400 |
| reference_id | You cannot provide existing reference id | 400 |




## Customer Webhook

### Setting Customer Webhook URL
<br/> Set <a name="customer_webhook">Webhook URL</a> to get order updates on your server.

#####A. Setting Customer Webhook URL:
1. Sign in to Shipox system as admin and go to Customers section. Find your customer, click on his ID and go to Finance Settings;
2. Select Contract Owner in dropdown list and submit the Contract Owner section;
3. On the Company section enter your company name and submit;
4. You will see opened more sections, find EndPoint input field in the Company Endpoint section and paste your Webhook URL and press submit.
#####B. Setting up Endpoint on your server which accepts Post request:
1. Set the endpoint to get the request body data as raw content of json type;
2. Here is the sample of json data:


            {
              "order_number": "1111111117",
              "reference_id": "1070171717",
              "status": "accepted",
              "note": "The order 1111111117 was created for test",
              "date": "2020-10-03T14:57:45.058Z",
              "customer_id": 171717,
              "driver": {
                "id": 111777,
                "name": "Aki Ahmed",
                "phone": "+971333333333",
                "email": "test_Aki@gmail.com"
              }
            }
                              
_Note: Driver object will appear only when the driver is assigned to the order!_


##Typical Workflow for Consuming APIs

1. Get the token in [Authorization](#/reference/0/authorization).
2. Find the country id in [Countries API](#/reference/0/countries).
3. Find the city id or code in [Cities API](#/reference/0/cities).
4. Get the neighborhood in [Neighborhoods API](#/reference/0/neighborhoods) if it is necessary.
5. Get the list of service types in [Service Types API](#/reference/0/service-types).
6. Find the appropriate package price in [Package Prices](#/reference/0/package-prices).
7. Gather the customer and parcel information.
8. And finally [Create the Order](#/reference/0/creating-order-v-2).
9. Then you can [Track the Order](#/reference/0/order-tracking).
10. Get the [AWBZ Label](#/reference/0/awbz-label).


## Authorization [/api/v1/customer/authenticate]

Shipox.com provides REST API to interact with its system. To use authenticated API endpoints 
you have to call Authorization API endpoint below and get your JWT token from response in 
the field named id_token. This token will then be included for other authenticated API 
requests in the request header. The token is valid for 24 hours from that time you received it.
**After token expiration you should call Authorization API to renew the token.**

_Add token in next requests headers._

_Note: This is for test purposes only!_


### Authorization [POST]

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            
    + Body
    
            {
                "username": "customer@Shipox.com.ae",
                "password": "12345678Ae",
                "remember_me": true
            }
            
+ Response 200 (application/json)
    
        {
            "data": {
                "id_token": "12eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJhYmFoYTIwQGdtYWlsLmNvbSIsInVzZXJJZCI6NzU1MzIzLCJleHAiOjE1NDg0MDI5NjB9.-0PLwe8jOV_vjKpRg5iumtlSXtLOfBG4vefT86lhMOsHi88btQY2hSTraUGKfnlYiQ79bBW6PFOnISHKNXZNmWw12",
                "user": {
                    "marketplace_id": 1,
                    "user_id": 123123,
                    "login": "customer@Shipox.com",
                    "version": 0,
                    "first_name": "Name ",
                    "last_name": null,
                    "email": "customer@gmail.com",
                    "activated": true,
                    "languages": "english",
                    "phone": "+971333333333",
                    "full_name": "Customer ",
                    "valid_phone": true
                }
            },
            "status": "success"
        }
        
        
        
      
      
## Countries [/api/v2/customer/countries{?page,size,search}]  

<br/> List Countries for indicating the pickup or drop-off country id.<br/>


+ Parameters
    + page (number, optional) - The page number, by default it is set to 0
        + Default: 0
    + size (number, optional) - The size of the page, by default it is set to 20, max value 200
        + Default: 20
    + search (number, optional) - The Search Key filter

### List All Countries [GET]

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers
    
            Accept: application/json
            Authorization: Bearer id_token
            
+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body
          
            {
              "data": {
                "total": 233,
                "list": [
                  {
                    "id": 229,
                    "name": "United Arab Emirates",
                    "description": "ae"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": 230,
                    "name": "United Kingdom",
                    "description": "gb"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": 231,
                    "name": "United States",
                    "description": "us"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "status": "success"
            }
            
      
      
