## Creating Order V2 [/api/v2/customer/order]

*Important*: Before you paste the following JSON to your request for <a name="order_creation">creating order</a>, please make sure to change the `city code` or `city id` and `courier_type` values to the ones matching for your account. 
If you decide to provide `city code` then you have to provide `country id`. 
If you decide to provide `city id`, then there is no need to provide the `country id`. 
If you decide to provide `latitude`&`longitude`, there is no need to indicate `city` and `country`.

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| sender_data | yes | Object | See <a href="#sender_resp">Sender and Recipient Data</a> section |
| recipient_data | yes | Object | See <a href="#sender_resp">Sender and Recipient Data</a> section |
| dimensions | yes | Object | See <a href="#dimensions">Dimensions Data</a> section |
| package_type | yes | Object | <a href="#package">See Package Type</a> section |
| charge_items | yes | Array | See <a href="#charge_items">Charge Items</a> section |
| recipient_not_available | yes | String | Possible values: `do_not_deliver`, `leave_at_door`, `leave_with_concierge`. Note: if the payer is `recipient` then this value should be `do_not_deliver`. E.g. The order has a COD to be collected, and the recipient is not available, then it should not be delivered. |
| payment_type | yes | String | Possible Values: `credit_balance`, `cash`, `wallet`, `paypal`,`stripe`,`ottu`,`credit_card`. For B2B customers, this value should be:  `credit_balance` |
| payer | yes | String | Possible values: `recipient`, `sender` |
| parcel_value | no | double | The price or approx value of the parcel to be sent |
| fragile | no | Boolean | Indicate if the item is fragile for lean transportation |
| note | no | String | Short description of the item(s) |
| piece_count | no | Integer | Number of items |
| force_create | no | Boolean | Must provide this as `true` to overcome our cut off times |
| is_dangerous | no | Boolean | true/false |
| reference_id | no | String | ID generated by your own System for the parcel. It can be used to search for the parcel or tracking. However, your parcel will also be assigned Shipox.com AWB, which is the main AWB |
| logistic_type | no | String | One of <b>REGULAR</b>, <b>REVERSE</b>. By default <b>REGULAR</b> |
| price_calculation_type | no | String | One of <b>TOTAL_WEIGHT</b>, <b>BOX_WEIGHT</b>, <b>BOX_COUNT</b>, <b>TOTAL_VOLUME</b>. By default <b>TOTAL_WEIGHT</b> |
| supplier_id | no | Integer | id of the courier |
| customer_id | no | Integer | id of the customer |
| parent_customer_id | no | Integer | id of the parent customer |
| sub_customer_id | no | Integer | id of the sub customer |
| duty_type | no | String | One of <b>DDU</b>, <b>DDP</b>. By default <b>NULL</b>. |
| boxes | no | Array | See <a href="#order_box">Order box Data</a> section |


### <a name="sender_resp">Sender and Recipient Data</a>

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| adress_type | yes | String | Possible values: `residential`, `business`. The purpose is to prevent late, day off or holiday delivery attempts to business addresses. |
| name | yes | String | Sender/recipient full name |
| email | no | String | Sender/recipient email address |
| phone_code | no | String | Sender/recipient phone country code |
| phone | no | String | Sender/recipient phone number |
| second_phone | no | String | Sender/recipient phone number |
| third_phone | no | String | Sender/recipient phone number |
| postcode | no | String | Postcode |
| apartment | no | String | Apartment number/code |
| building | no | String | Building number/name/code |
| street | no | String | Street name |
| landmark | no | String | Landmark |
| city | yes | Object | See <a href="#city_object">City object</a>. Possible values can be retrieved from the <a href="#cities">Cities API</a> If you provide lat&lon skip this field |
| country | yes | Object | See <a href="#country_object">Country object</a>. Possible values can be retrieved from <a href="#countries">Countries Api</a> If you provide lat&lon skip this field |
| neighborhood | no | Object | See <a href="#neighborhood_object">Neighborhood object</a>. Possible values can be retrieved from the <a href="#neighborhoods">Neighborhoods API</a> |
| lat | no | double | Latitude, if you provide city details and skip this, the coordinate is set to the city center |
| lon | no | double | Longitude, if you provide city details and skip this, the coordinate is set to the city center |
| saudi_address_id | no | string | Short address code for Saudi Post Office |

