### <a name="dimensions">Dimensions</a>
Shipox.com utilizes volumetric weight and actual weight to calculate the cost of the package delivery. You can just pass weight if you do not want to use volumetric weight. If both weight and volume details(width, height, length and unit) are provided then volumetric weight is calculated and compared to the provided weight. Whichever greater is used to calculate the delivery cost.

Volumetric weight is calculated based on the formula below:
`
Volumetric Weight Metric = width * height * length / 5000
Volumetric Weight Imperial = width * height * length / 139
`

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| weight | Yes | Double | The total actual weight of the items to be delivered |
| width | No | Double | Positive fractional/whole number |
| height | No | Double | Positive fractional/whole number |
| length | No | Double | Positive fractional/whole number. Length can be omitted for 2 dimensional items |
| unit | No | String | Possible values: `metric`, `imperial` |
| domestic | No | Boolean | If true, the weight rounding up is incremented by 1, (e.g. if the volumetric weight is 1.25 kg it is rounded to 2 kg). If false, the weight rounding up is incremented by 0.5 (e.g if the volumetric weight is 1.26 kg it is rounded to 1.5 kg) |

### <a name="package">Package Type</a>
| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| id | yes | integer | Possible Values can be retrieved from the <a href="#service_type">Service Types API</a> |
| package_price | yes | Object | Possible Values can be retrieved from the <a href="#package_rules">Package prices API</a> |

### <a name="charge_items">Charge Items</a>

Charge items keep the information about charges for parcel(COD) and delivery service(service_custom).
You should provide charge amount, charge type (cod and service_custom) and the payer.

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| charge_type | yes | String | Possible Values: `cod`, `service_custom`, `additional_charge` |
| paid | no | Boolean | Indicate if charge is paid or not |
| charge | yes | Double | The amount to be paid |
| additional_charge_id | no | Integer | Id of the additional charge, required if `charge_type`='additional_charge' |
| additional_charge_amount | no | BigDecimal | Amount of additional charge, required if `charge_type`='additional_charge' |
| payer | yes | String | Possible Values: `recipient`, `sender`, `client` |

***Note*: If you don't want your recipient to pay for delivery charge, provide `service_custom` charge type as 0, so that on the AWB label the charge for delivery will be shown as 0.**



