## Creating Order V3 with Box data [/api/v3/customer/order]

*Important*: Before you paste the following JSON to your request for <a name="order_creation">creating order</a>, please make sure to change the `city code` or `city id` and `courier_type` values to the ones matching for your account. 
If you decide to provide `city code` then you have to provide `country id`. 
If you decide to provide `city id`, then there is no need to provide the `country id`. 
If you decide to provide `latitude`&`longitude`, there is no need to indicate `city` and `country`.

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| sender_data | yes | Object | See <a href="#sender_resp_v3">Sender and Recipient Data</a> section |
| recipient_data | yes | Object | See <a href="#sender_resp_v3">Sender and Recipient Data</a> section |
| dimensions | yes | Object | See <a href="#dimensions_v3">Dimensions Data</a> section |
| package_type | yes | Object | <a href="#package_v3">See Package Type</a> section |
| charge_items | yes | Array | See <a href="#charge_items_v3">Charge Items</a> section |
| recipient_not_available | yes | String | Possible values: `do_not_deliver`, `leave_at_door`, `leave_with_concierge`. Note: if the payer is `recipient` then this value should be `do_not_deliver`. E.g. The order has a COD to be collected, and the recipient is not available, then it should not be delivered. |
| payment_type | yes | String | Possible Values: `credit_balance`, `cash`. For B2B customers, this value should be:  `credit_balance` |
| payer | yes | String | Possible values: `recipient`, `sender` |
| parcel_value | no | double | The price or approx value of the parcel to be sent |
| fragile | no | Boolean | Indicate if the item is fragile for lean transportation |
| note | no | String | Short description of the item(s) |
| force_create | no | Boolean | Must provide this as `true` to overcome our cut off times |
| reference_id | no | String | ID generated by your own System for the parcel. It can be used to search for the parcel or tracking. However, your parcel will also be assigned Shipox.com AWB, which is the main AWB |
| agent | no | String | Agent name |
| boxes | yes | Object | Parcel's boxes and their content. See <a href="#boxes_resp_v3">Boxes Data</a> |
| manifest | no | String | Manifest number |
| placed_storage_address | no | String | The address where the parcel will be located for pick up |


### <a name="sender_resp_v3">Sender and Recipient Data</a>

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| adress_type | yes | String | Possible values: `residential`, `business`. The purpose is to prevent late, day off or holiday delivery attempts to business addresses. |
| name | yes | String | Sender/recipient full name |
| passport_series | no | String | Sender/recipient passport series |
| passport_number | no | String | Sender/recipient passport number |
| email | no | String | Sender/recipient email address |
| apartment | no | String | Apartment number/code |
| building | no | String | Building number/name/code |
| street | no | String | Street name |
| landmark | no | String | Landmark |
| city | yes | Object | See <a href="#city_object_v3">City object</a>. Possible values can be retrieved from the <a href="#cities">Cities API</a> If you provide lat&lon skip this field |
| country | yes | Object | See <a href="#country_object_v3">Country object</a>. Possible values can be retrieved from <a href="#countries">Countries Api</a> If you provide lat&lon skip this field |
| neighborhood | no | Object | See <a href="#neighborhood_object_v3">Neighborhood object</a>. Possible values can be retrieved from the <a href="#neighborhoods">Neighborhoods API</a> |
| lat | no | double | Latitude, if you provide city details and skip this, the coordinate is set to the city center |
| lon | no | double | Longitude, if you provide city details and skip this, the coordinate is set to the city center |

### <a name="boxes_resp_v3">Boxes Data</a>

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| description | yes | String | Description of box |
| height | yes | Integer | Box height (sm) |
| length | yes | Integer | Box length (sm) |
| weight | yes | Integer | Box weight (kg) |
| width | yes | Integer | Box width (sm) |
| line_items | yes | Object | Items inside the box. See <a href="#box_line_items_v3">Line Items Data</a> |

### <a name="box_line_items_v3">Line Items Data</a>

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| name | yes | String | Name of item |
| ean13_code | yes | String | Thirteen-digit EAN standard code |
| origin_country | yes | String | Origin country |
| price_per_unit | yes | Double | Per item quantity price |
| price | yes | Double | Item price |
| quantity | yes | String | Item quantity |
| tax_code | yes | String | Tax code |
| desc | yes | String | Description of item |
| weight | yes | Integer | Item weight (kg) |

### <a name="city_object_v3">City object<a/> 

    + Sample
           
        {
            "city": 
                {
                  "id": 4,
                  "code": "dubai",
                  "name": "Dubai"
                }
        }
            
        
        
### <a name="country_object_v3">Country object<a/>
    
    + Sample
    
        {
            "country": 
                {
                  "id": 229
                }
        }
        
        
        
        
### <a name="neighborhood_object_v3">Neighborhood object<a/>
    
    + Sample
    
        {
            "neighborhood": 
                {
                  "id": 22,
                  "name: "Industrial Area"
                }
        }
            


### <a name="dimensions_v3">Dimensions</a>
Shipox.com utilizes volumetric weight and actual weight to calculate the cost of the package delivery. You can just pass weight if you do not want to use volumetric weight. If both weight and volume details(width, height, length and unit) are provided then volumetric weight is calculated and compared to the provided weight. Whichever greater is used to calculate the delivery cost.

Volumetric weight is calculated based on the formula below:
`
Volumetric Weight Metric = width * height * length / 5000
Volumetric Weight Imperial = width * height * length / 139
`

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| weight | Yes | Double | The total actual weight of the items to be delivered |
| width | No | Double | Positive fractional/whole number |
| height | No | Double | Positive fractional/whole number |
| length | No | Double | Positive fractional/whole number. Length can be omitted for 2 dimensional items |
| unit | No | String | Possible values: `metric`, `imperial` |
| domestic | No | Boolean | If true, the weight rounding up is incremented by 1, (e.g. if the volumetric weight is 1.25 kg it is rounded to 2 kg). If false, the weight rounding up is incremented by 0.5 (e.g if the volumetric weight is 1.26 kg it is rounded to 1.5 kg) |

### <a name="package_v3">Package Type</a>
| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| id | yes | integer | Possible Values can be retrieved from the <a href="#service_type">Service Types API</a> |
| package_price | yes | integer | Possible Values can be retrieved from the <a href="#package_rules">Package prices API</a> |

### <a name="charge_items_v3">Charge Items</a>

Charge items keep the information about charges for parcel(COD) and delivery service(service_custom).
You should provide charge amount, charge type (cod and service_custom) and the payer.

| Name | Required | Type | Description |
| ---- | -------- | ---- | ----------- |
| charge_type | yes | String | Possible Values: `cod`, `service_custom` |
| paid | no | Boolean | Indicate if charge is paid or not |
| charge | yes | Double | The amount to be paid |
| payer | yes | String | Possible Values: `recipient`, `sender`, `client` |

***Note*: If you don't want your recipient to pay for delivery charge, provide `service_custom` charge type as 0, so that on the AWB label the charge for delivery will be shown as 0.**



